#: acpi.cpp:62
msgid ""
"This panel provides information about your system's ACPI implementation\n"
"and lets you have access to some of the extra features provided by ACPI"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:65
msgid ""
"NOTE: the Linux ACPI implementation is still a 'work in progress'.\n"
"Some features, in particular suspend and hibernate are not yet available\n"
"under 2.4 - and under 2.5 some particular ACPI implementations are still\n"
"unstable, these check boxes let you only enable the things that work "
"reliably.\n"
"You should test these features very gingerly - save all your work, check "
"them\n"
"on and try a suspend/standby/hibernate from the popup menu on the battery "
"icon\n"
"in the panel if it fails to come back successfully uncheck the box again.\n"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:73 apm.cpp:70
msgid ""
"Some changes made on this page may require you to quit the laptop panel\n"
"and start it again to take effect"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:77 apm.cpp:74
msgid "Enable standby"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:79 apm.cpp:76
msgid ""
"If checked this box enables transitions to the 'standby' state - a temporary "
"powered down state"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:83 apm.cpp:80
msgid "Enable &suspend"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:85 apm.cpp:82
msgid ""
"If checked this box enables transitions to the 'suspend' state - a semi-"
"powered down state, sometimes called 'suspend-to-ram'"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:90
msgid "Enable &hibernate"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:92
msgid ""
"If checked this box enables transitions to the 'hibernate' state - a powered "
"down state, sometimes called 'suspend-to-disk'"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:97
msgid "Use software suspend for hibernate"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:99
msgid ""
"If checked this box enables transitions to the 'hibernate' state - a powered "
"down state, sometimes called 'suspend-to-disk' - the kernel 'Software "
"Suspend' mechanism will be used instead of using ACPI directly"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:109
msgid "Enable &performance profiles"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:111
msgid ""
"If checked this box enables access to ACPI performance profiles - usually OK "
"in 2.4 and later"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:115
msgid "Enable &CPU throttling"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:117
msgid ""
"If checked this box enables access to ACPI throttle speed changes - usually "
"OK in 2.4 and later"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:121
msgid ""
"If the above boxes are disabled then there is no 'helper'\n"
"application set up to help change ACPI states, there are two\n"
"ways you can enable this application, either make the file \n"
"/proc/acpi/sleep writeable by anyone every time your system boots \n"
"or use the button below to make the KDE ACPI helper application\n"
"set-uid root"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:128 apm.cpp:96
msgid "Setup Helper Application"
msgstr ""

#: acpi.cpp:130
msgid "This button can be used to enable the ACPI helper application"
